                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.731/137: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-10-11T11:00:00+01:00">October 11, 1939—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 11—7:05 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2415. Department’s rush 1210, October 10, 7 p.m. French authorities state that
                    they have just discovered that they are obliged to notify the Bureau Des Unions
                    Internationales Télégraphiques at Bern today of their decision to permit the use
                    of the six codes mentioned in my 2203. I shall inform you as soon as the French
                    authorities have received approval of their decision from Bern probably [today?]
                    or tomorrow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
